{
  "$comment": "VAPP-120 typed host ACTIONS ×4: every Exponential MCP operation is a host function an app may call, `exponential.<noun>.<op>` (the apps noun's ops included; the `exponential_sessions_send` verb tool = `exponential.sessions.send`; `session_self` and `guide_write` are not offered: they need an agent's session), run by the client's app host as a tools/call on the instance's MCP as the viewer (the `harness.mcp` transport, arguments = {op, …args}; no `op` for the verb tool). A package lists what it calls in `functions` (an exact name or a `prefix*` pattern: `exponential.issues.*`); the SDK denies anything else. GRANTS (the 2026-10-24 ruling, a conservative default): only a team OWNER (`grantRole`; `canGrantActions(role)`) sets or changes an app's grants, the app's creator gets no grant power from creating it; a DESTRUCTIVE operation (`destructiveWords`: a word of the tool name or op is delete, merge, close, end, remove, trash; `actionDestructive`, `actionGrantable` = not destructive) can NEVER be granted: the server refuses it, every host ignores a stored grant for it (`grantAllows` is false), and it always shows the consent card with the operation's words, for every viewer; the settings row of a destructive action shows `copy.tools.always` in place of the switch, a non-owner sees the switches disabled. `grantableCases` and `canGrantCases` replay ×4 beside `grantCases` (which carry: an owner's grant skips the card for a non-destructive op, a destructive op ignores a grant). `apps.granted_tools` (synced on the apps shape, a list of exact function names) = what the app may run as the viewer WITHOUT asking: the app's SETTINGS page (web + desktop; phones have no app settings) shows a `copy.tools` group under the records line with one row per declared function (`declaredActions`: patterns expand against `functions`), the display row's title (contract `expToolDisplay`, `<noun>_<op>`) + the function name muted + a Switch (an owner; others see it disabled; a destructive action shows `copy.tools.always` instead), `copy.tools.none` when the package declares none, `copy.tools.hint` under the title. The server (`apps.update`, an owner only) accepts a grant only for a non-destructive action the HEAD package declares, and every new version (upsert, restore) drops the grants it no longer declares: a grant is a choice about the current package, never inherited by a later version that re-declares the action. A typed call's `op` is the NAME's: an `op` key in the args never changes the operation (×4). CONSENT: a declared, ungranted call shows the consent card worded for the operation (`actionConsent`: title `Allow this surface to <title, lower-cased><subject>?` where subject = the arg named by the row's `subjectKey` when it is a string; the destructive variant when a word of the tool name or op is delete, merge, close, end, remove, trash; the arguments block = the args without `op`), Allow runs it ONCE; a granted call runs without a card; `harness.mcp` keeps the generic copy and always asks. The TS reference `app-actions.ts` is replayed by desktop `domain::app_actions`, iOS `AppActions.swift`, Android `AppActions.kt` (`parseCases`, `grantCases`, `declaredCases`, `consentCases`); `functions` is the ×4 list (the web gates it against its noun table).",
